{0 FAQ}


Does the driver support TLS and bolt+s?
- Current session connection path does not enable TLS and connects to 127.0.0.1. Use non‑TLS [bolt://] locally or through a tunnel. TLS enablement is planned.

Can I run queries concurrently on one session?
- A session serializes requests (one in‑flight exchange). Create multiple sessions for parallel queries.

How do I stream large results?
- Use [Session.run_stream]/[run_stream_records] with [~fetch_size]. Iterate via [fetch_next(_records)] and stop when [exhausted] is true.

How do I set fetch size?
- Pass [~fetch_size] to streaming functions, or for strict queries [Session.run(_records)] will loop with repeated PULLs; you can also pass [~fetch_size] there.

How do I decode nodes and relationships?
- Use [Record.at_node]/[at_relationship] or [Extract.node]/[Extract.relationship]. Node props are in [Value.StringMap].

Why are field names missing?
- Some Cypher returns (e.g., unlabeled projections) produce driver records without usable field names. Always alias fields ([AS name]).

What happens after a query failure?
- Outside transactions, the driver auto‑issues [RESET] and subsequent queries proceed. Inside a transaction, call [rollback] to clear failed state.
